tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xRule"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false | FocusGuideRuleOptions<TDatum>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusGuideX"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full-height rule at the focused x coordinate"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yRule"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false | FocusGuideRuleOptions<TDatum>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusGuideY"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full-width rule at the focused y coordinate"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"marker"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false | FocusGuideMarkerOptions<TDatum>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabled"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dot at the focused x/y coordinate"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xLabel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false | FocusGuideLabelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabled"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Label outside the x edge"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yLabel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false | FocusGuideLabelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabled"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Label outside the y edge"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMotionDefinition<TDatum>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enter, retarget, and exit policy"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule options provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineCap"},{"type":"text","value":". Marker options provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radius"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"},{"type":"text","value":". Paint and numeric\nrule or marker values may be datum visual channels."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Label options provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"side"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offset"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paddingX"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paddingY"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radius"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"background"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fontSize"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fontWeight"},{"type":"text","value":". A formatter receives the typed semantic value and a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FocusGuideLabelFormatContext"},{"type":"text","value":" containing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ point }"},{"type":"text","value":", the active "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand its original datum reference."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"focus-and-motion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and motion"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guide candidates participate in scale inference but do not enter\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartScene.points"},{"type":"text","value":", pointer hit testing, callbacks, or tooltip rows. Focus\nresolves the selected candidate under stable structural keys. The first target\nenters at its final coordinate, later targets update the same rule, marker, and\nlabel nodes, and clearing focus exits those nodes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary matching uses the original object reference, or the primitive value\nplus source position for primitive rows. Candidate ownership is structural;\nkeys such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a:point"},{"type":"text","value":" remain distinct rather than being interpreted as\na hierarchy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static SVG, Canvas, and native surfaces snap to the resolved focus target. The\noptional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/motion"},{"type":"text","value":" SVG renderer applies "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"},{"type":"text","value":", preserves\nspring velocity through rapid retargets, and handles reduced motion and\nteardown. A focus guide composes with the default focus ring; set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusRing: false"},{"type":"text","value":" only when its marker replaces that indicator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused(mark, { retarget: true })"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes the same structural behavior\nfor custom compositions. Normal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused"},{"type":"text","value":" marks keep their existing\npre-rendered visibility behavior when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retarget"},{"type":"text","value":" is omitted."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"focus-and-motion","text":"Focus and motion","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`focusGuideX` and `focusGuideY` render ordinary scene nodes only for the active\nfocus target. Import them from the exact optional subpath:\n\nFor an unsnapped x/y value pair with no datum focus target, use\n[`continuousCursor`](../focus-and-interaction.md#continuous-cursor) instead.\n\n```ts\nimport { focusGuideX } from '@tanstack/charts/focus/guide'\n\nfocusGuideX(rows, {\n  id: 'cursor',\n  x: 'period',\n  y: 'value',\n  z: 'series',\n  key: 'id',\n  yRule: {},\n  marker: {},\n  xLabel: { format: (period) => period },\n  yLabel: { format: (value) => String(value) },\n  motion: {\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 240, damping: 22 },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`focusGuideX` enables the vertical x rule by default. `focusGuideY` enables the\nhorizontal y rule. Configure both rules on either mark for a crosshair.\n\n```ts\nfunction focusGuideX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FocusGuideOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction focusGuideY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FocusGuideOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n```\n\n## Options\n\n| Option   | Type                                       | Default                | Meaning                                      |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`     | `string`                                   | Layer-derived          | Stable mark and motion owner                 |\n| `x`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`             | Required               | Semantic x value and guide position          |\n| `y`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`             | Required               | Semantic y value and guide position          |\n| `z`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | No group               | Series identity retained on guide points     |\n| `key`    | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred               | Candidate datum identity                     |\n| `match`  | `ChartFocusMatch`                          | `'primary'`            | Focus selection used to choose candidates    |\n| `xRule`  | `false \\| FocusGuideRuleOptions<TDatum>`   | `{}` for `focusGuideX` | Full-height rule at the focused x coordinate |\n| `yRule`  | `false \\| FocusGuideRuleOptions<TDatum>`   | `{}` for `focusGuideY` | Full-width rule at the focused y coordinate  |\n| `marker` | `false \\| FocusGuideMarkerOptions<TDatum>` | Disabled               | Dot at the focused x/y coordinate            |\n| `xLabel` | `false \\| FocusGuideLabelOptions`          | Disabled               | Label outside the x edge                     |\n| `yLabel` | `false \\| FocusGuideLabelOptions`          | Disabled               | Label outside the y edge                     |\n| `motion` | `ChartMotionDefinition<TDatum>`            | None                   | Enter, retarget, and exit policy             |\n\nRule options provide `stroke`, `strokeOpacity`, `strokeWidth`,\n`strokeDasharray`, and `lineCap`. Marker options provide `radius`, `fill`,\n`fillOpacity`, `stroke`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth`. Paint and numeric\nrule or marker values may be datum visual channels.\n\nLabel options provide `format`, `side`, `offset`, `paddingX`, `paddingY`,\n`radius`, `background`, `color`, `stroke`, `strokeWidth`, `fontSize`, and\n`fontWeight`. A formatter receives the typed semantic value and a\n`FocusGuideLabelFormatContext` containing `{ point }`, the active `ChartPoint`\nand its original datum reference.\n\n## Focus and motion\n\nGuide candidates participate in scale inference but do not enter\n`ChartScene.points`, pointer hit testing, callbacks, or tooltip rows. Focus\nresolves the selected candidate under stable structural keys. The first target\nenters at its final coordinate, later targets update the same rule, marker, and\nlabel nodes, and clearing focus exits those nodes.\n\nPrimary matching uses the original object reference, or the primitive value\nplus source position for primitive rows. Candidate ownership is structural;\nkeys such as `a` and `a:point` remain distinct rather than being interpreted as\na hierarchy.\n\nStatic SVG, Canvas, and native surfaces snap to the resolved focus target. The\noptional `@tanstack/charts/motion` SVG renderer applies `motion`, preserves\nspring velocity through rapid retargets, and handles reduced motion and\nteardown. A focus guide composes with the default focus ring; set\n`focusRing: false` only when its marker replaces that indicator.\n\n`whenFocused(mark, { retarget: true })` exposes the same structural behavior\nfor custom compositions. Normal `whenFocused` marks keep their existing\npre-rendered visibility behavior when `retarget` is omitted.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Focus Guide Marks\ndescription: Render datum-bound focus rules, markers, and axis labels with stable renderer-neutral motion.\n---\n\n`focusGuideX` and `focusGuideY` render ordinary scene nodes only for the active\nfocus target. Import them from the exact optional subpath:\n\nFor an unsnapped x/y value pair with no datum focus target, use\n[`continuousCursor`](../focus-and-interaction.md#continuous-cursor) instead.\n\n```ts\nimport { focusGuideX } from '@tanstack/charts/focus/guide'\n\nfocusGuideX(rows, {\n  id: 'cursor',\n  x: 'period',\n  y: 'value',\n  z: 'series',\n  key: 'id',\n  yRule: {},\n  marker: {},\n  xLabel: { format: (period) => period },\n  yLabel: { format: (value) => String(value) },\n  motion: {\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 240, damping: 22 },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`focusGuideX` enables the vertical x rule by default. `focusGuideY` enables the\nhorizontal y rule. Configure both rules on either mark for a crosshair.\n\n```ts\nfunction focusGuideX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FocusGuideOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction focusGuideY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: FocusGuideOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n```\n\n## Options\n\n| Option   | Type                                       | Default                | Meaning                                      |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`     | `string`                                   | Layer-derived          | Stable mark and motion owner                 |\n| `x`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`             | Required               | Semantic x value and guide position          |\n| `y`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`             | Required               | Semantic y value and guide position          |\n| `z`      | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | No group               | Series identity retained on guide points     |\n| `key`    | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred               | Candidate datum identity                     |\n| `match`  | `ChartFocusMatch`                          | `'primary'`            | Focus selection used to choose candidates    |\n| `xRule`  | `false \\| FocusGuideRuleOptions<TDatum>`   | `{}` for `focusGuideX` | Full-height rule at the focused x coordinate |\n| `yRule`  | `false \\| FocusGuideRuleOptions<TDatum>`   | `{}` for `focusGuideY` | Full-width rule at the focused y coordinate  |\n| `marker` | `false \\| FocusGuideMarkerOptions<TDatum>` | Disabled               | Dot at the focused x/y coordinate            |\n| `xLabel` | `false \\| FocusGuideLabelOptions`          | Disabled               | Label outside the x edge                     |\n| `yLabel` | `false \\| FocusGuideLabelOptions`          | Disabled               | Label outside the y edge                     |\n| `motion` | `ChartMotionDefinition<TDatum>`            | None                   | Enter, retarget, and exit policy             |\n\nRule options provide `stroke`, `strokeOpacity`, `strokeWidth`,\n`strokeDasharray`, and `lineCap`. Marker options provide `radius`, `fill`,\n`fillOpacity`, `stroke`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth`. Paint and numeric\nrule or marker values may be datum visual channels.\n\nLabel options provide `format`, `side`, `offset`, `paddingX`, `paddingY`,\n`radius`, `background`, `color`, `stroke`, `strokeWidth`, `fontSize`, and\n`fontWeight`. A formatter receives the typed semantic value and a\n`FocusGuideLabelFormatContext` containing `{ point }`, the active `ChartPoint`\nand its original datum reference.\n\n## Focus and motion\n\nGuide candidates participate in scale inference but do not enter\n`ChartScene.points`, pointer hit testing, callbacks, or tooltip rows. Focus\nresolves the selected candidate under stable structural keys. The first target\nenters at its final coordinate, later targets update the same rule, marker, and\nlabel nodes, and clearing focus exits those nodes.\n\nPrimary matching uses the original object reference, or the primitive value\nplus source position for primitive rows. Candidate ownership is structural;\nkeys such as `a` and `a:point` remain distinct rather than being interpreted as\na hierarchy.\n\nStatic SVG, Canvas, and native surfaces snap to the resolved focus target. The\noptional `@tanstack/charts/motion` SVG renderer applies `motion`, preserves\nspring velocity through rapid retargets, and handles reduced motion and\nteardown. A focus guide composes with the default focus ring; set\n`focusRing: false` only when its marker replaces that indicator.\n\n`whenFocused(mark, { retarget: true })` exposes the same structural behavior\nfor custom compositions. Normal `whenFocused` marks keep their existing\npre-rendered visibility behavior when `retarget` is omitted.\n"}
